# QA squad — Lead + Coder + Reviewer + QA
#
# The Trio pattern plus a dedicated QA pass: the Lead plans, the Coder
# implements, the Reviewer checks the change, and QA verifies the result
# actually works end to end before it's considered done. Good for anything
# where "it compiles and the reviewer liked it" isn't enough on its own.
#
# This file uses ${Provider1..3}/${Model1..3} placeholders instead of naming
# a specific provider -- `lmctl quickrun` fills them in with YOUR configured
# providers/models (recorded by `lmctl init`), so this exact file works
# whether you have one provider or several. Four members share three
# provider slots (QA reuses Provider1/Model1) -- that's fine, a slot can back
# more than one member. See
# https://lmctl.com/lmctl/docs/manuals/teamfile-format for what a _MEMBER_
# line means and how to customize this after it's seeded.

_MEMBER_ alias=Lead     provider=${Provider1} model="${Model1}"
_MEMBER_ alias=Coder    provider=${Provider2} model="${Model2}"
_MEMBER_ alias=Reviewer provider=${Provider3} model="${Model3}"
_MEMBER_ alias=QA       provider=${Provider1} model="${Model1}"
